Subject: [PATCH] test(drawings): the W23 assembly sheet's parts list, counted
 by hand (#11773)

A small test assembly from plain shapes, built by one command script in
tests/fixtures/w23-assembly-sheet/: a base plate, four screws on it, and a
holder placed twice with a block and two screws in each.

Four tests in bom_tests.rs check assembly.bom against the hand counts:
parts only, the first level, all levels and the holder's own list; item
numbers through a renumber, a new part, undo and redo, a deleted holder
and save and reopen in both formats; the screw purchased; the holder a
phantom. No production code changes.

